      "writtenOn": "2022-03-22T22:52:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems safer to do it this way, since this will catch if a hooktype isn\u0027t being linked for some reason (it will fail to link with a pretty clear error). I also think this ends up being no more complex on balance, since searching for the correct type would have some complexity and doubly so if we wanted to be clever with something like binary search.\n\nSince this is all build-time computation, I\u0027m happy to trade a small amount of ROM for pointers to reduce the runtime cost.",
